  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The bullet enters your shoulder just underneath the collarbone, exiting your back through the shattered shoulder blade. Either the bullet or a bone fragment pierces the top of your lung, which partly collapses as air and blood enters the pleural space.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> Gain @Condition[Fatigued] (2). Because it’s only a rather minor pneumothorax you’ll remove one @Condition[Fatigued] Condition each week spontaneously as the lung inflates itself back again. You also suffer a @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.4lj1ik958mbgAlaF]{Broken Bone (Minor)}. </p><p>No Extraction is necessary.</p>"
    },
